     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Tuesday, March 23, 2021 at 5:51:54 AM UTC-4 marc.kery wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr;font-family:Tahoma;color:#000000;font-size:12pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Dear all,</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Michael Schaub and I have written a textbook about integrated population models (IPMs), which\r\n<i>Academic Press</i> will publish later in 2021. The book will have 650 pages and two parts: in the first part, we describe the theory of IPMs in 10 chapters, while in the second part, we present 11 shorter chapters with\r\n case studies, and then there is also a short chapter with Conclusions. The IPM book is written in the same style as our earlier BPA book (and the AHM books) and we use JAGS as our (Bayesian) model fitting engine. There will also be an R package called &#39;IPMbook&#39;,\r\n for which we are again deeply indebted to Mike Meredith.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Right now, we expect chapter proofs to be sent by AP between 5-14 May. We would be very happy if some people could volunteer to check a chapter or two for errors, both in the text and also by running all the code and seeing whether it works.\r\n Here is a list of all the chapters in the book. If you feel that you would have time (perhaps 1 day max) in an approximate time window of 5-21 May to deal with this rapidly (e.g., return within 5 days after receipt), then please let us know what chapter(s)\r\n you would like to proof-read and –code-run.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b>Chapter list</b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p>\r\n<table style=\"width:318.05pt;margin-left:2.75pt;border-collapse:collapse\" width=\"1060\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" border=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n<td style=\"width:22.05pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"74\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<br>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width:296.0pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"987\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"color:black\">Part I: Theory of Integrated Population\r\n Models</span></b></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n<td style=\"width:22.05pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"74\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:right\" align=\"right\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"DE-CH\">0</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width:296.0pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"987\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"DE-CH\">Preface</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n<td style=\"width:22.05pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"74\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:right\" align=\"right\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"DE-CH\">1</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width:296.0pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"987\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"DE-CH\">Introduction</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n<td style=\"width:22.05pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"74\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:right\" align=\"right\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"DE-CH\">2</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width:296.0pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"987\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\">Bayesian statistical modeling using\r\n JAGS</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n<td style=\"width:22.05pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"74\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:right\" align=\"right\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"DE-CH\">3</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width:296.0pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"987\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\">Introduction to stage-structured population\r\n models</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n<td style=\"width:22.05pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"74\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:right\" align=\"right\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"DE-CH\">4</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width:296.0pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"987\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\">Components of integrated population\r\n models</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n<td style=\"width:22.05pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"74\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:right\" align=\"right\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"DE-CH\">5</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width:296.0pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"987\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\">Introduction to integrated population\r\n models</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n<td style=\"width:22.05pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"74\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:right\" align=\"right\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"DE-CH\">6</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width:296.0pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"987\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\">Benefits of integrated population modeling</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n<td style=\"width:22.05pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"74\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:right\" align=\"right\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"DE-CH\">7</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width:296.0pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"987\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\">Assessment of integrated population\r\n models</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n<td style=\"width:22.05pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"74\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:right\" align=\"right\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"DE-CH\">8</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width:296.0pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"987\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\">Integrated population models with density-dependence</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n<td style=\"width:22.05pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"74\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:right\" align=\"right\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"DE-CH\">9</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width:296.0pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"987\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"DE-CH\">Retrospective\r\n population analyses</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n<td style=\"width:22.05pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"74\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:right\" align=\"right\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"DE-CH\">10</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width:296.0pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"987\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"DE-CH\">Population\r\n viability analysis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n<td style=\"width:22.05pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"74\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<br>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width:296.0pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"987\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<br>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n<td style=\"width:22.05pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"74\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<br>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width:296.0pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"987\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"color:black\">Part II: Case studies: Integrated\r\n Population Models in practice</span></b></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n<td style=\"width:22.05pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"74\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:right\" align=\"right\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"DE-CH\">11</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width:296.0pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"987\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"DE-CH\">Woodchat\r\n shrike</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n<td style=\"width:22.05pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"74\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:right\" align=\"right\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"DE-CH\">12</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width:296.0pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"987\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\" lang=\"DE-CH\">Peregrine\r\n falcon</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n<td style=\"width:22.05pt;padding:0in 3.5pt 0in 3.5pt;height:15.0pt\" width=\"74